Constructor VS Destructor:
Constructor(__init__): A special method automatically called when an object is created. It is used to initialize instance variables.
A constructor is a special method that is automatically executed when an object is created. It is used to initialize the object's data members.

TYPES OF CONSTRUCTOR:
1. Default Constructor: No parameters except self.
2. Parameterized Constructor: Accepts additional parameters.

USES:
1. Initialize object data
2. Assign default values
3. Open files or database connections
4. Prepare object for use

Destructor(__del__): A special method automatically called when an object is destroyed. It is used to release resources sucha as files, network 
                    connections etc.



